   "issue": "`integral_betaShape` re-proves Euler's beta value from scratch (induction on `b` with the recursion at lines 188-195). TauCeti, a declared dependency (code/lakefile.toml:16), already has it: `TauCeti.integral_rpow_mul_one_sub_rpow (ha : 0 < a) (hb : 0 < b) : \u222b t in (0:\u211d)..1, t ^ (a - 1) * (1 - t) ^ (b - 1) = beta a b` (upstream/TauCeti/TauCeti/Analysis/SpecialFunctions/Beta.lean:125); the `succ`-branch `key` is exactly the natural-exponent instance of `TauCeti.integral_rpow_mul_one_sub_rpow_add_one_right` (same file, line 158).",
